WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.101
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:04.236
is an Emmy-nominated performer
and best-selling author.

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:07.640
Please welcome back to the show
our friend Amy Sedaris.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.642
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:22.221 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.623
Welcome back.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.260
-Oh, wow!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.127
Hi, Seth.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.663
-You look fantastic, as always.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.298
What a wonderful choice
you've made,

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.401
your sartorial style unrivaled.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.770
-Well, I was a little limited
on what I could wear

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.205
because John Early is --

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.307
-The fantastic John Early,
wonderful comedian.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.742
-Well, I own
the apartment above me,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.644
and he's staying there,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.746
overstaying his visit
for like two weeks.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.249
But all my getting-ready dresses
are up there.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.649
So I was like,
I don't want to go up there

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:51.851
when someone's staying up there

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:55.121
because then I see
an unmade bed, underpants.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.124
-Oh, so you're not going
out of respect for them.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.492
You don't want
to spin yourself out.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.826
-I don't want to spin myself out

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:04.096
and see an extra pair of shoes
that don't belong to him.

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:07.367
So anyway, this is what I had.
But I love this dress.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.236
-So this isn't even in your
first choice line of dresses.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.371
-No. I've had this for five
years and I've never washed it.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:14.307
Shoo, shoo, shoo,
shoo, shoo, shoo!

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.042
How dare you?

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.477
-He'll text me messages

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.045
and say, "I crawled down
the fire escape

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.181
and watched you sleep
last night."

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.549
-That's what your upstairs --
-Yeah.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.916
This is what John Early told me.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.018
Then he's like, "When I told
the doorman I was leaving,

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.653
they burst into tears."

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.555
And then I'll run into him
on the street,

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:32.092
and it's 1:00 in the afternoon,
and he's like, "I just woke up."

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.226
And I'm like,
"John, what is going on?"

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:36.463
He's panfrying croissants
up there.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.097
-Oh, my God.
-But he's a good guest.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.231
-I don't know.

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:40.399
It doesn't sound like
he's a good guest.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.768
-He is. He is. He is.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:44.637
-Now, I like doing a check-in
every time you're here.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.506
about your dear rabbit...
-Tina Bunny.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:48.708
-...Tina Bunny.
-Yes.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.576
-Now, Tina Bunny
is a male rabbit.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.544
-Mm-hmm.
-But you have had --

00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:54.347
The first time you were
on the show nine years ago,

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.381
we discussed Tina.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.216
-I brought Tina home that night,

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.385
and then I was freaking out
that I made a mistake.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.621
This is my third rabbit.
They told me it was a girl.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.723
Then four years later,
they told me it was a boy.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.091
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.392
-So you are a fair--

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.494
You consider yourself somewhat
of an expert on rabbits?

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:09.863
-I am an expert.
I have a badge.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.831
I go to people's houses.
I educate them.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.600
-But it took you four years
to know that Tina was a boy.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:15.868
-It's tough.
Yeah.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.503
They were trying to insert
a catheter and they said,

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:20.306
"Amy, this is a boy bunny."

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.907
-I will say, you cannot tell
from the photo, but this is --

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.709
-Look at him.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.111
He's chewed a few things.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.178
-He has chewed a few things.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:28.748
But that is his right
as a rabbit.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.216
-Yes.
-Getting up there in age.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.918
How long does a rabbit go?

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.685
-Well, my last rabbit
lived to be 12,

00:02:33.685 --> 00:02:34.954
which is old for a bunny.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.356
Tina's 10, but all of a sudden,
out of nowhere,

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:39.492
he started wetting my bed,
peeing in my bed.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.694
I don't know why.
I think it's behavioral.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.062
-You don't think it's age?

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:46.665
-No, because I have experience
with senior bunnies

00:02:46.665 --> 00:02:48.267
and I think
his kidneys are fine.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:51.304
But -- So I ordered -- I went
to a surgical supply store

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.940
and I ordered a bunch
of those reusable medical,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.841
you know, bed pads, whatever.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.176
Yeah.
-Yeah. Okay.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:59.812
-But they arrived to my
apartment building unwrapped

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.815
in just, like, saran that said,
"Amy Sedaris, Apartment 4C,"

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.517
so everyone in my building

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.186
thinks I'm wetting my bed,
easily,

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:10.189
'cause I'll be down in
the laundry room folding them.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:13.259
But anyway,
he stopped peeing in my bed.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.195
Now he just goes --
he just leaves little droppings.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.598
They look like peppercorns.
It's no big deal.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.832
So I safety-pin --

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.634
If you have a pad
that's 48 by 48,

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.236
that'll cover a queen-size bed.

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.805
But they're hard to find.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:29.107
And so I safety-pinned it on top
of my, you know, bedspread

00:03:29.107 --> 00:03:30.376
so in case it happens.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.511
It happens between 2:30
and 3:00 in the morning.

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:33.913
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.348
-He's just really dialed in
to that one certain window.

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:38.451
-I don't know why.
I mean, I went through --

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.919
During the strike, you know,

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.054
I went through
a George Michael hole.

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:43.923
I'm post-hole now,
but I was like --

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.925
-George Michael the singer?
-Yes.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.393
-Yeah, okay.
-The "Wham!" documentary.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.661
Then I got obsessed with that.
Then I got obsessed with him.

00:03:49.661 --> 00:03:52.899
And maybe I was just so,
you know, obsessed with it

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:56.535
that I was pulling focus from
my attention to Tina, maybe,

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:57.970
and he was just getting even.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.572
-I see.
-My acupuncturist --

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:03.843
-You're saying that maybe Tina
was wetting the bed on purpose

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.111
because you were
too into George Michael?

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.546
-Maybe, maybe.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:09.715
-And then my acupuncturist said,
"Well, did you ask Tina?

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:11.584
Did you talk to Tina?"

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.751
And I'm like, "Yes."

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:14.653
And he's like,
"What did Tina say?"

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:15.988
And I'm like, "Nothing."

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.923
And I haven't been back
to that acupuncturist.

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:19.525
-Yeah, that doesn't seem like

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:23.129
it's an acupuncturist's
place to say.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.297
-Oh, my God.
So, yeah, that was something.

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:26.699
-Did you buy or are you renting

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:27.800
the apartment
next door to yours?

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.969
-Okay, so then another apartment

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.204
opened up in my building
right next door,

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:34.206
and I thought, "Well, this
would be a good investment."

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:36.108
So I just use it
as a storage unit.

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:40.479
So I keep my hay in there,
luggage and petticoats.

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:42.448
-Okay.
-But I do have Wi-Fi.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.715
-Well, that's great.
Yeah.

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:46.985
-Fudge Pot. Fudge Pot's
the name of my Wi-Fi.

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:48.454
-You're giving away your Wi-Fi?

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.788
Oh, that's just the name
of the Wi-Fi.

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:51.624
You're not giving out the
password, just the name of it.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.827
Fudge Pot and then do your best.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.962
So these are the sort of things
you would see over there.

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:58.998
That's a small amount of hay.
This is the sort of --

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:01.367
I guess it's good
for you to say there's Wi-Fi,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.435
'cause I think if you walked
into an apartment full of hay,

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:06.138
you might think it was
an Amish person.

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:08.541
There might not be Wi-Fi
or a need for Wi-Fi.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.676
-It reeks of goats, trust me.

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:12.244
But I can't imagine --

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:14.513
I mean, to combine
my apartment --

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:17.417
It's crazy to have
three apartments in one building

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.218
and they're not attached,
but, you know,

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:22.655
the idea of having to, you know,
put a hole in my wall...

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.256
You know, since my husband died,

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:27.960
I don't have anybody who can
take care of that stuff for me.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.562
I don't want to think
about knobs and wallpaper.

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:32.998
-Who wants to think
about knobs and wallpaper?

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:35.167
But you're living
your best life.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:37.736
Knobs and wallpaper is just
going to slow you down.

00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:39.304
-It's crazy.
-Now, when your neighbors

00:05:39.304 --> 00:05:41.640
see giant boxes of hay
getting delivered,

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.675
do you think they look at that

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.711
the same way they look
at the pee pads?

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.180
-That I'm a stoner.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.348
They probably think it's just
weed coming out of my house.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:50.482
Big boxes of weed.

00:05:50.482 --> 00:05:52.818
-Yeah, giant see-through
plastic bags of hay.

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.420
-Well, you said
you had a goat before.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.788
You have goats?
-I've never had a goat.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.590
My father-in-law had a goat.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.691
-Same thing.
-Yeah, no.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.293
-Really?
-Yeah, I inherited it.

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:03.663
It was part of my dowries
that I inherited.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:05.197
He was like, "Will you take
my daughter's hand?"

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:08.367
And I'm like,
"Not without the goat."

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.802
-I always wanted a goat.

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.671
-Yeah, I don't think you do.

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.673
-No, I know, yeah.

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:15.975
-You know, he misses
his goat a great deal

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.209
and talks about it lovingly.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:19.378
I did not find the goat
had a lot of charisma.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.079
-What was the goat's name?
-Raisin.

00:06:21.079 --> 00:06:23.516
-[ Laughs ]
That's cute.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:25.518
-And based on what
they leave everywhere...

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:26.752
-Yeah.
-Not a bad --

00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:28.120
Peppercorn would have been
a good name.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.489
-Peppercorns or capers.
It's no big deal.

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:33.358
-Capers. Capers would be
a very funny name for a goat.

00:06:33.358 --> 00:06:35.761
-Oh, yeah. Capers.
It would be adorable.

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:39.231
-Capers would be a great name
for a kid's book about goat --

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:41.199
a goat who pulled crimes.

00:06:41.199 --> 00:06:43.001
-Oh, yes. Oh, yes.
-Or solved them.

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:44.536
Capers the goat.
-Yes.

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:46.371
-Yeah, and he'd be
a goat burglar.

00:06:46.371 --> 00:06:47.673
It would be like a cat burglar,

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:49.242
but you would, like,
definitely hear them.

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.409
-I would buy that book.
-Alright, great.

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:51.510
Well, let's work on it together.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.811
I have a bunch more
questions for you.

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:55.081
We'll be right back with more
from Amy Sedaris.

